for a search warrant under the Crime Commission Act 2012, section 17(2)
or a digital evidence access order in connection with the search
warrant—an authorised officer, or

for the purpose of preventing or controlling a
public disorder in a particular area described in the authorisation,
or

persons at, or seeking to enter or leave, a
public place at which a sporting event, concert or other artistic performance,
dance party, parade or other entertainment is being held,

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the order to be affixed to or near the entrance of the
premises.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the application notice to be affixed to or near the
entrance of the premises.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the notice to be affixed to or near the entrance to the
premises.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the withdrawal notice to be affixed to or near the
entrance of the premises.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the application notice to be affixed to or near at least
one of the entrances to the land.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the order to be affixed to or near at least one of the
entrances to the land.

if personal service cannot be effected promptly,
by causing a copy of the notice to be affixed to or near at least one of the
entrances to the land.

Date of commencement of Sch 2.28, 17.7.2009, sec 2 (2);
date of commencement of Sch 3, 17.7.2009, sec 2
(1).
